===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|droschel|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|drōscala}}. The modern consonantism is [[Central German|Central]] and [[Low German]] (compare {{etyl|gml|de}} {{term|drōsle|lang=gml}}, from  {{etyl|osx|de}} {{term|thrōsla|lang=osx}}).

====Noun====
{{de-noun|f||Drosseln}}

# [[thrush]] {{gloss|songbird of the family [[Turdidae]]}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|de|Drosselbart}}
* {{l|de|Singdrossel||throstle, song thrush}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|drozzel}}, from {{etym|goh|de}} {{m|goh|drozza}}. Akin to {{etyl|ang|-}} {{m|ang|þrote}}.

